{
  "Displays one page at a time from a horizontal set. Users move between pages with a swipe or drag, and you can navigate with `next()`, `previous()` and `goTo()`, or with [Tabs](/tabs), a [Stepper](/stepper) or buttons bound to the same value. It works like the panels of a tab control without the tab strip.": "",
  "Using MultiView with a Stepper": "",
  "The `View` children are the pages. `value` is the visible view, identified by its `key` or index, and `x-model` provides two-way binding. In this example, a `Stepper` shares the value, so pressing a step and swiping a page both update it. A page is created when it first becomes visible (`lazy`).": "",
  "Lazy creation and keeping views alive": "",
  "`lazy`, the default, creates a view when it first becomes visible and then keeps it. `keepAlive={false}` disposes what a view's `content` created while it is hidden and recreates it next time. JSX children are always kept, as in `Tabs`.": "",
  "Create the component with `new`, add views with `add()` and `insert()`, and remove them with `remove()`. `loop` wraps around at the ends, and `animated={false}` shows the next view immediately.": "",
  "A `group` named “Pages” in the kit language. If a page has several, give each one its own `label`.": "",
  "A `group` named by its `title`, or “Page 2 of 3”. Views out of sight are hidden from assistive technology and the keyboard (`inert`), so Tab moves only within the visible view.": "",
  "Swiping requires a finger or a mouse, so also provide keyboard access through `Tabs`, a `Stepper` or buttons bound to the same `value`, as the examples do.": "",
  "The multi-view. `data-swipe` when dragging is enabled, `data-dragging` during a drag, and `data-still` with `animated` off.": "",
  "The frame that clips the views and the track that moves inside it (`data-dragging`, `data-no-motion`).": "",
  "A view (`aria-hidden` and `inert` when hidden).": "",
  "Units: the frame (`swipeable`, `dragging`) and a view.": "Unit'ler: çerçeve (`swipeable`, `dragging`) ve görünüm.",
  "The gap between views, visible during a drag.": "",
  "MultiView props": "MultiView prop'ları",
  "The visible view, identified by its `key` or index. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "The first view follows the last, and the transition wraps around instead of running back across the views in between.": "",
  "Lets a finger or pointer drag the views. A drag that is far or fast enough moves to the next view.": "",
  "Animates the transition between views. `false` shows the next view immediately.": "",
  "Creates a view when it first becomes visible and then keeps it. A view's own `lazy` takes precedence.": "",
  "With `false`, disposes what a view's `content` created while the view is hidden. A view's own `keepAlive` takes precedence.": "",
  "View props": "View prop'ları",
  "“Page 2 of 3”": "“Sayfa 2 / 3”",
  "The accessible name of the view.": "",
  "Identifies the view in `value`. The JSX `key` is also read.": "",
  "Content created when the view first becomes visible, in addition to the JSX children.": "",
  "The view's own settings. `undefined` inherits from the multi-view.": "",
  "A hidden view takes no space and is skipped. A disabled view is skipped by `next()` and `previous()`, and `goTo()` rejects it.": "",
  "Occurs before the visible view changes (`from`, `to`, `fromView`, `toView`, `byUser`). Set `cancel = true` to keep the current view.": "",
  "Occurs after the visible view changes (`index`, `view`, `previous`, and `byUser` for a swipe, as opposed to code).": "",
  "The views in order, including hidden ones.": "",
  "The visible view and its index, or `null` and -1 if there is none.": "",
  "The number of views.": "",
  "Moves to the next or previous view that is visible and enabled. Returns `false` at an end without `loop`, or if the change was canceled.": "",
  "Moves to a view by index, key or `View` object. `onSelecting` is raised first. A view's own `select()` does the same.": "",
  "Adds a view at the end or at an index. A view from another multi-view moves here.": "",
  "Removes a view and disposes it. The display moves to an adjacent view.": ""
}
